  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "new_object",
    "file": "libredwg/src/in_dxf.c",
    "description": "Root cause is ownership/lifetime misuse of DXF pair string data in new_object: a heap string from dxf_read_pair (pair->value.s) is attached into the created DIMENSION entity/common fields, but the same pair is immediately released via dxf_free_pair at the loop tail (line ~12015). Later, dwg_free_common_entity_data (via dwg_free_DIMENSION_ANG2LN) frees that aliased pointer again, causing double-free. So the bug is in parsing/assignment code in new_object that stores non-duplicated pair memory into persistent object state while still freeing the pair.",
    "conditions": "Trigger by supplying DXF ENTITIES content (here a DIMENSION/ANG2LN path) with string-bearing group codes that are copied by pointer into entity/common data (e.g., fields freed by common_entity_data.spec such as color/name-like strings). During parse, new_object frees each Dxf_Pair; during final dwg_free, the same pointer is freed again. Input must drive successful object creation so stale pointer survives until dwg_free."
  },
